KG42.register("source_edge_archive-7fd908646364bcb29907cc46",{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E002","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E002","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C004"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"KG31-c38847500f58498d","target":"COMP-276b46f772c03e0a","source_occurrence_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::V::execution.energy_trade","target_occurrence_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","source_unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::execution.energy_trade","target_unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. | Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. | Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. | The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"9d8d5f0ad604ce38e9ca6cceb9b1a5261468acde37ff5213e62bb77489646f6a","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Contract performance, exchange or delivery conditions in this mechanism: ESP computes internal buying/selling prices from supply-demand ratio and grid tariffs; prosumers iteratively reschedule; preserve service-fee and balance conditions.","target_definition":"Price updates/signals and participant decision feedback in this mechanism: ESP computes internal buying/selling prices from supply-demand ratio and grid tariffs; prosumers iteratively reschedule; preserve service-fee and balance conditions.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Local surplus-PV sharing is conditional on successful convergence of iterative price-signal coordination. In the successful branch the internal price is settled and prosumers agree to share; the failure branch leaves direct utility-grid trading available. Scope: Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. Condition: The iterative internal-price coordination process converges to a fixed point within Algorithm 1's iteration limit; k > K is the stated failure branch.","expression":"if k > K then unsolvable and PV prosumers trade with utility grid directly; else the internal price is settled as Pr and PV prosumers agree to share the surplus PV energy in the microgrid","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-K","v141-c-R003-Pr"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-28","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3575 Algorithm 1 Initialize T P i, P i, ,i = [1, 2, . .","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Algorithm 1\nInitialize \\mathbf{TP}_{i}, \\mathbf{P}_{i}, i = [1, 2, \\ldots, n]\nfor k = 1 to K do\n Collect NP_i from each U-EMS, randomly sample δ_{i,ω}^{h} of M realizations to generate NP_{i,ω_m};\n Calculate TSP and TBP: TSP_{ω_m}^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i,ω_m}^{h}, NP_{i,ω_m}^{h} \u003c 0 ; TBP_{ω_m}^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i,ω_m}^{h}, NP_{i,ω_m}^{h} ≥ 0\n Calculate SDR: SDR_{ω_m}^{h} = \\frac{TSP_{ω_m}^{h}}{TBP_{ω_m}^{h}}\n Central setting price: Pr_{ω_m}^{h} = f(SDR_{ω_m}^{h}),\n Local optimization at each U-EMS of PV prosumer:\n x_i = arg\\min_x \\frac{1}{M} \\sum_{m=1}^{M} \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\left( Pr_{i,ω_m}^{h}\\left( x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}\\left( 1 + δ_{i,ω_m}^{h} \\right) \\right) + α_i · \\left( x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h} \\right)^{2} \\right)\n if \\left\\| Pr - Pr_{old} \\right\\| ≤ ε then stop iteration end if\nend for\nif k > K then The energy sharing model is unsolvable, and then PV prosumers trade with utility grid directly.\nelse The internal price is settled as Pr, PV prosumers agree to share the surplus PV energy in the microgrid.\nend if"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-29","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p08-c1r3__v141-a-M01-validation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 8. Load/power curves of the typical day in summer: (a) prosumers’ PV powe load curve and net po","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"If the iterative process converges to a ﬁxed point after a ﬁnite number of iterations, the energy sharing zone with internal price Pr converges and all PV prosumers can beneﬁt from this feasible solution. Otherwise, it is divergent, the energy sharing model is unsolvable and the PV prosumers still can trade with the utility grid directly."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. | Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. | Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. | The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E002","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"conditional_on","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"]},"paper_scope_note":"Retain the positive and negative net-power branches, ESP organizational responsibilities, cost valuation, and the shared service fee sub-item; the iterative price, final price, and grid trading after failure cannot be treated as identical."}});
